        <item>
            <title>2.1.0</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:01:50 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>144</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.1.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<p><em>Settings, rearranged into one long, well-signposted page.</em></p>
<ul>
  <li>Settings now lives in the Scribe menu (⌘,), where Mac apps keep it, and the gear has left the top bar.</li>
  <li>Settings is larger, with a list of sections down the side that follows you as you scroll: Reading, Today &amp; the stack, Library, Categories, Appearance &amp; motion, Shortcuts, and Updates.</li>
  <li>Set your reading defaults there: typeface, text size, column width and line spacing, each on a slider.</li>
  <li>See where your library is kept, with a button to show it in Finder, and a list of every keyboard shortcut.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/AdamDWalker/scribe-releases/releases/download/v2.1.0/Scribe-2.1.0.zip" length="9138293" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="cUR6QzK25UY5MH4Ox4k1c24jBb16V2KyrV6TjJ1M9FVZ6t0gMYf5VAfDSy1/wDNFDorp+eeTw2kNZ0juLvOFAw=="/>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title>2.0.2</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:23:12 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>142</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.0.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<p><em>Departments are now Categories, and search lets go when you’re done.</em></p>
<ul>
  <li>Departments are now called Categories, and subdepartments subcategories. Your categories, themes and filing are just as you left them.</li>
  <li>⌘F from any tab opens the Catalogue with the search field ready to type in.</li>
  <li>Escape, or a click anywhere else, puts the search field down without losing what you typed, and the other tabs work on the first click.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/AdamDWalker/scribe-releases/releases/download/v2.0.2/Scribe-2.0.2.zip" length="9065869" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="S9FkH3l4lNx8U2oh+n1dYugS3mkCW0/Quv4wZX7sYmrsLepRpeIiTOMxcQzTHlYwIumlNy+rfJ2a+/shB3iXCQ=="/>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title>2.0.1</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:04:23 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>140</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.0.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<p><em>The first round of snags from living with 2.0.</em></p>
<ul>
  <li>The backlog deals its cards off a pile of books on the table, and each card lands a little higher or lower than its neighbours.</li>
  <li>Opening a book is one smooth movement again: the title page no longer slides in beside the cover.</li>
  <li>The reader’s … menu has lost what was left over from before the redesign. Articles and books keep their notes in the margin, so Show Notes is now for PDFs only.</li>
  <li>Click a highlight to remove it from the note that opens.</li>
  <li>Details no longer repeats the page colour, which lives in Aa.</li>
  <li>The menu bar says Scribe, with a capital S.</li>
  <li>Scribe now looks for updates every hour, not once a day.</li>
  <li>And this: what’s changed, shown after each update.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/AdamDWalker/scribe-releases/releases/download/v2.0.1/Scribe-2.0.1.zip" length="9061974" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="f5lNDgIio3tnxTWm+Oqt2z523I607DGV1XbxhXGLFQBjFqoz1STZzS+elbgv2lSv9Yqh2nwwJDWsMOoFsNPuCQ=="/>
        </item>
